From e537afa4825f3f1926600ea6d30524affa82d67e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:52:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Type the registration inputs, cut the aliases, split out dev
 tooling (issue 9)

Registration took many input shapes and silently dropped what it did not
understand, there were dozens of alias names, and the README described a
CLI that does not exist.

- Each registration function now takes one documented, typed shape
  (arrays of ids or { id } objects, arrays of { from, to } edges, a
  name-to-spec map for actions) through overloads. Wrong shapes and
  unknown keys fail with INVALID_REGISTRATION and the right call, in both
  throw and collect mode, instead of being ignored.
- Drop the cloneFrom/from synonyms for template.
- Keep the canonical camelCase set, its snake_case mirror and the
  matching instance methods. Remove every other alias, the DynamicTree
  type, and the instance methods addScreens, addEdges and clone.
- unregisterScreens/unregisterEdges reject selectors that are not ids.
- Move the source scanner and NavGraphWatcher into packages/devtools, a
  private package outside the published files. Fix scan-app.js, which had
  stray shell lines and did not parse, and remove its unused --graph
  option. Remove the scan script.
- README, llms.txt, AGENTS.md and CHANGELOG describe the above; the false
  CLI and diff claims are gone.
